 "derivation": "MEASURED from the owner's 2026-27 timetable workbooks (PEQ-YEAR-3 \u00a71), not derived from planners and not chosen by ruling. Period unit 40 min, read off the timetable's own time column and cross-checked against the Teacher Timetable header. Per room, on the printed classification rule: Build (a) 0 slots / (a)+(b) 8; Grow (a) 2 / 8; Launch (a) 4 / 8. The working basis is (a)+(b) = 8 slots = 320 min = 5.333 h/wk, identical across the three rooms because the timetable makes it so - no lane inherits another's rate. The floor differs and is reported beside it: Build has NO explicitly ASDAN-labelled slot at all, Grow has 1.333 h/wk, Launch 2.667 h/wk. Three slots are owner-decision and counted in neither figure (the DT-vs-Behaviour-Intervention disagreement between the two workbooks), plus one borderline label. See _passpq/TIMETABLE_2026-27.md for the source cell of every row.",
